{
	"name": "Casting Style",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/unholy/hands-cloud-light-pink.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Each warcaster learns how to engage in combat casting very early in their career. At 1st level, choose one of the following casting styles:</p><p></p><h2>Defensive</h2><p>When wearing any armor or using the @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.ip8c3zrbrngrx1oe]{Mage Armor} spell, you gain an additional +1 bonus to AC.</p><p></p><h2>Deflector</h2><p>When you have one hand free, you may add your proficiency bonus to your AC until the end of the current turn as a reaction to being attacked.</p><p></p><h2>Long Range</h2><p>You gain a +1 bonus to ranged spell attack rolls against targets at least 30ft away from you.</p><p></p><h2>Offhand</h2><p>So long as you are wielding a weapon or focus in one hand, you do not have disadvantage when making ranged spell attacks while in a hostile creature’s threatened area.</p><p></p><h2>Overwhelming</h2><p>You may reroll one damage die per turn when you deal damage with your cantrips but must use the second number even if it is lower.</p><p></p><h2>Spellbinding</h2><p>You gain a +1 to spell save DC for your warcaster cantrips.</p>",
